description: Core project context, always active
alwaysApply: true
---

- This is Name Origins: a name etymology + cross-language cognate explorer.
- Data is aggregated from Wikidata (graph backbone) + Behind the Name
  (enrichment text) into our own Postgres. Never call either source from a
  user-facing request path — reads only hit our DB.
- MVP scope = etymological naming traditions only (Western/Biblical/
  Greco-Roman-descended, plus Hebrew/Arabic/Sanskrit-rooted names where
  covered). Compositional (Chinese/Japanese/Korean) and circumstantial
  (Akan/Yoruba-style) traditions are out of scope — do not build features
  or schema that quietly force-fit them into the etymological model. See
  `cultural-scope.mdc`.
- Prefer the simplest solution that fits current scale. Do not add
  services/infra not already listed in `stack.mdc` without flagging it.
